# The build context is every tracked file plus .git. `go build` stamps
# the main module version from git (Go 1.24 and later): the tag on a
# tagged commit (v1.32.0), a pseudo-version between tags
# (v1.32.1-0.20260925001332-10674814d276), and a +dirty suffix when the
# context differs from the commit. A tracked file that is left out of the
# context counts as a deleted file, and an untracked file that is not
# ignored counts as a new one. Either stamps +dirty.
#
# So this file excludes only local state that git does not track. The
# repository .gitignore and .git/info/exclude travel with .git and apply
# in the build. A global excludes file (core.excludesFile) does not, so a
# path that only it ignores must also be listed here.

# Local editor, shell and agent state
**/.claude/
.serena/
.idea
.vscode/
.mcp.json
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.bash_profile
.bashrc
.profile
.zprofile
.zshrc
.ripgreprc
.rumdl_cache/
